{
  "id": "long-vowels",
  "title": "Long Vowels",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Holding a vowel for one extra mora changes meaning. Vowel length is phonemically significant in Japanese : two otherwise identical words can differ only in how long a vowel is held."
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_table",
      "columns": [
        "short",
        "romaji",
        "long",
        "romaji ",
        "difference"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "short": "おじさん",
          "romaji": "ojisan",
          "long": "おじいさん",
          "romaji ": "ojiisan",
          "difference": "uncle vs grandfather"
        },
        {
          "short": "ここ",
          "romaji": "koko",
          "long": "こうこう",
          "romaji ": "kōkō",
          "difference": "here vs high school"
        },
        {
          "short": "おばさん",
          "romaji": "obasan",
          "long": "おばあさん",
          "romaji ": "obaasan",
          "difference": "aunt vs grandmother"
        },
        {
          "short": "ビル",
          "romaji": "biru",
          "long": "ビール",
          "romaji ": "bīru",
          "difference": "building vs beer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_title",
      "content": "How Long Vowels Are Written"
    },
    {
      "type": "pattern",
      "lines": [
        "Hiragana: repeat the vowel (or **お + う** for the ō sound)",
        "Katakana: use **ー** (chōonpu)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_table",
      "columns": [
        "japanese",
        "romaji",
        "english"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "japanese": "おかあさん",
          "romaji": "okaasan",
          "english": "mother"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "こうこう",
          "romaji": "kōkō",
          "english": "high school"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "コーヒー",
          "romaji": "koohii",
          "english": "coffee"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "スーパー",
          "romaji": "suupaa",
          "english": "supermarket"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "content": "The ー mark only appears in katakana. In hiragana words, the long vowel is spelled out explicitly (ああ, おう, etc.). The difference between おじさん and おじいさん is one extra い : easy to miss in handwriting."
    }
  ]
}